&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Holy Cow (Vingt Dieux)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Louise Courvoisier, 2024, 92 min.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Register &lt;a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/screening-of-holy-cow-vingt-dieux-tickets-1408798437049?aff=oddtdtcreator"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following the sudden death of his father, a hard-partying dairy farmer, 18-year-old Totone (Cl&amp;eacute;ment Faveau) is reluctantly thrust into adulthood in Louise Courvoisier&amp;rsquo;s warm and gently comic debut feature. Premiering in the Un Certain Regard section at the Cannes Film Festival, the film charts Totone&amp;rsquo;s unconventional path to responsibility as he takes a job at a nearby dairy farm, falls for the farmer&amp;rsquo;s daughter, and hatches a plan to save his family by entering a regional cheese competition&amp;mdash;with a 30,000 Euro prize for the best Comt&amp;eacute;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rooted in the landscapes and rhythms of rural Jura, where Courvoisier herself was raised, the film blends a cast of non-professional local actors with an affectionate, lived-in realism. Equal parts coming-of-age fable and pastoral portrait, this charming and flavorful story celebrates both the emotional messiness of growing up and the earthy traditions of French agricultural life&amp;mdash;sure to delight cinephiles and cheese lovers alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Watch the trailer &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/Q55naIp7PCI?si=aM4AOYljcW8EfGU1"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This screening is made possible by the generous support of Albertine Cin&amp;eacute;math&amp;egrave;que.&lt;/p&gt;

