&lt;p&gt;The last workshop of the semester will be an easy going session where we will learn how to solder our own contact mics!&amp;nbsp;A piezo contact mic is a type of microphone that picks up vibrations directly from solid objects by using a piezoelectric effect sensor. Unlike a traditional microphone that captures sound waves in the air, a contact mic is placed directly onto a surface, such as an instrument or a wall, and records the sounds produced by its vibrations. No previous experience is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
