&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation Alchemy: A Book Talk with Lori Glover&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/innovation-alchemy-a-book-talk-with-lori-glover-tickets-1972847684532?aff=oddtdtcreator" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REGISTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://datascience.columbia.edu/news/2025/new-dsi-leader-to-grow-columbias-partnerships-with-industry-and-expand-research-impact/" target="_blank"&gt;Lori Glover&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, incoming Chief of Strategic Alliances at the Data Science Institute, will share insights from her book&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://innovationalchemy.net/" target="_blank"&gt;Innovation Alchemy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and her experience leading global academic&amp;ndash;industry partnerships. She will explore how ideas move from research to real-world impact, what enables truly symbiotic collaborations, and how universities can position themselves to lead in a rapidly evolving innovation landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With industry investment accelerating and research ecosystems expanding in the AI era, this session will bring together DSI&amp;rsquo;s community of faculty, researchers, and industry practitioners to examine what effective partnership models look like in practice today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The program will be moderated by&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://datascience.columbia.edu/people/garud-n-iyengar/" target="_blank"&gt;Garud Iyengar&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, Avanessians Director of the Data Science Institute and Professor of Industrial Engineering and Operations Research, Columbia Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Lori Glover:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Glover comes to Columbia after more than a decade at MIT, where she built the Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Laboratory&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://cap.csail.mit.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;(CSAIL) Alliances program&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;from the ground up. She has created one of the most successful university-industry partnership programs in the country, which includes focused efforts on FinTechAI@CSAIL, Machine Learning Applications@CSAIL, and the MIT Future of Data, Trust &amp;amp; Privacy. The CSAIL Alliances program currently engages more than 150 companies globally and supports a broad portfolio of research, talent, and innovation collaborations at MIT&amp;rsquo;s largest lab, home to more than 900 active projects.&lt;/p&gt;

